## 🎯 2. Project Objective

* To integrate **solar PV energy** with a **small hydropower plant** to maintain generation capacity during the dry season.
* To design an **ANN–Fuzzy controller** optimized using **Eel Optimization (EO)** and **Manta Ray Optimization (MRO)** for efficient **reservoir water-level management** and **power stabilization**.
* To ensure **cost-effective, stable, and reliable renewable power generation** by coordinating the PV array, pump, inverter, and reservoir system.

---

## ⚙️ 3. System Architecture Overview

### Components:

| Component               | Description                                                                    |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **PV Array**            | 1500 V DC array producing ~170 MW (AC) via inverters.                          |
| **Inverter**            | Converts DC (1500 V) → AC (690 V RMS) → stepped up to 13.8 kV via transformer. |
| **Step-up Transformer** | 690 V → 13.8 kV to connect to the generator bus.                               |
| **Hydro Generator**     | 200 MVA, 13.8 kV synchronous generator; pf = 0.9; P ≈ 180 MW.                  |
| **Upper Reservoir**     | 10 m high, 300,000 m² area, 3.3 × 10⁶ m³ total volume.                         |
| **Lower Reservoir**     | 12 m high, 250,000 m² area, 3.0 × 10⁶ m³ total volume.                         |
| **Pump-Motor Set**      | 170 MW (AC), 0.9 pf lagging, draws ≈ 82 MVAr during pumping.                   |
| **Penstock**            | Conduit carrying flow between reservoirs.                                      |
| **Control Unit**        | ANN–Fuzzy controller optimized using EO and MRO.                               |
| **Load Bus**            | Connected to 13.8 kV main AC bus.                                              |

